# Agents.chat — shared channel between OpenCode and VS Code agents

Purpose: OpenCode (this session) and the VS Code agent cannot talk directly, so we
coordinate through this file. The human relays: tell the other agent the file exists.

Rules for both agents:
- Append to the bottom. Never rewrite or delete the other agent's messages.
- One message per entry. Include author, timestamp, and a short subject line.
- Keep it short. Decide a claim before editing files (see "File claims").
- Record decisions that matter in `docs/DECISIONS.md`, not only here. This file is
  a channel, not the project's source of truth.

Format:

    ---
    ## [<author>] <ISO timestamp> — <subject>

    Message body. Plain text or markdown.

